<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Ping of Zhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 770–720 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Ping of Zhou was the first king of the Eastern Zhou, reigning from 770 to 720 BCE. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanrong">Quanrong</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haojing">Haojing</a> and killed his father King You in 771 BCE, he moved the court east to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengzhou">Luoyi</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>) with the support of Jin, Zheng and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>. The move began a long decline of royal authority as the regional states grew stronger.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-ping-of-zhou.jpg" alt="King Ping of Zhou" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 冯梦龙、蔡元放 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%91%A8%E5%B9%B3%E7%8E%8B.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The decisive step came in 770 BCE, when Duke Xiang of Qin escorted <b>King Ping of Zhou</b> eastward after the sack of the western Zhou capital.</blockquote><a href="/empire/state-of-qin">State of Qin · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>You favoured his consort Bao Si and her son Bofu, and deposed Queen Shen and the crown prince <b>Yijiu</b>, who fled to his maternal grandfather, the Marquis of Shen.</blockquote><a href="/empire/western-zhou">Western Zhou · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Quanrong sacked Haojing in 771 BCE, <b>King Ping</b> moved the court east to Luoyi (Luoyang), under the protection of the State of Jin and the State of Zheng, beginning the Eastern Zhou.</blockquote><a href="/state/eastern-zhou">Eastern Zhou</a></li></ul></section>
